  "title": "Francis Drake's circumnavigation",
  "summary": "Francis Drake left Plymouth in 1577 with five ships to raid Spanish holdings on the Pacific coast of the Americas. Only the Golden Hind passed through the Strait of Magellan; it reached California in June 1579, crossed the Pacific, rounded the Cape of Good Hope and returned to Plymouth on 26 September 1580.",
  "when": {
    "start": {
      "year": 1577
    },
    "end": {
      "year": 1580
    },
    "precision": "day",
    "uncertainty": {
      "note": "History.com gives the departure as 13 December 1577, while the Drake Navigators Guild gives 15 November 1577 and a gale-forced return to port the next day. The Guild dates entering the Pacific to 6 September 1578, Valparaíso to 5 December 1578 and Drakes Bay to 17 June 1579; it gives the return as September 1580, History.com as 26 September 1580."
    },
